WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.554
The lasting lesson is simple: since gradient
sparsification only ever needs an approximate set of top gradients,

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:11.030
it should not pay for an exact selection algorithm.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.665
By swapping exact parallel prefix sum for direct
randomized hashing,

00:00:15.745 --> 00:00:17.506
DRAGONN turns a sequential,

00:00:17.586 --> 00:00:22.277
dependency-heavy compression step into an
embarrassingly parallel one,

00:00:22.357 --> 00:00:27.798
removes the overhead that had been cancelling out
sparsification's benefits, and,

00:00:27.878 --> 00:00:31.274
together with tensor selection and sparse decoding,

00:00:31.354 --> 00:00:37.000
makes gradient sparsification finally pay off at
scale without sacrificing accuracy.
